{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-sol","packSha":"a74b1d01c847e357ccb82f8fa866422da4f6f51db04a30969d86f2f19ea21424","packTokens":1766,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":205,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":493,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":916,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":39,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should authentication and authorization be applied to contract operations?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce authentication and authorization only where contracts/openapi.yaml explicitly declares them.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen if demo seeding runs more than once?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Repeated runs may insert duplicate copies of the sample rows.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"A pen may contain animals from multiple lots, but a feeding activity identifies a lot. How should a pen-level delivery be attributed when it serves multiple lots?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record a separate activity per lot, with each activity containing only that lot's share of the delivered feed.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What unit-conversion rule should be used when feed inventory, ration ingredients, and feeding quantities use different units?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Convert quantities to pounds for calculations and inventory deductions, treating a ton as 2,000 pounds; retain the entered units for display.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should implementation preserve any records that may already exist in the PostgreSQL App database while adding the contract's data model?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Preserve existing records and add the required model without resetting the database.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"The spec contains 14 requirements, estimated at about two runs of work. Should all 14 remain in this run, or should some scope be deferred?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 14 requirements in one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every HTTP operation in contracts/openapi.yaml at its declared path and method, with the specified schemas, status codes, media types, behavior, errors, and security, and expose a matching public OpenAPI document.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide sign-in, overview, and lot operations with the contract-defined account, procurement, pen allocation, lifecycle, weight, performance, financial, and recommendation information.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Provide inventory records, stock projections, movements, and validated receipts with entered units and pounds-normalized quantities and costs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Provide ration listing and creation with ingredient, nutrition, and cost information, plus optimization and explicit saving or assignment of optimization candidates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Provide dated feeding plans with pen, ration, planned quantity, status, and separate allocations for each lot served.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Provide feeding activity listing, creation, correction, and cancellation with calculated variances, ingredient consumption, costs, energy, and inventory deductions, reversing deductions on cancellation and rejecting insufficient stock without changing records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"For a delivery serving multiple lots, attribute only each lot's share to its distinct allocation and record a separate feeding activity containing only that lot's share.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Provide weight measurement listing, creation, and correction with updated metrics and weight trends, as well as yard summaries and a filterable feed-to-gain report with CSV and PDF exports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Provide contract-authorized account administration, procurement synchronization with record-level results, demo information, and a demo flow.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Require bearer authentication where the contract declares it, leave sign-in unauthenticated, and enforce role restrictions only where declared, returning the specified unauthorized and forbidden errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Persist contract-backed operational records in PostgreSQL through the configured ConnectionStrings:App connection, apply the required data model without deleting, resetting, or changing pre-existing records, and preserve created or updated records across restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Run SeedData.Run only when Seed:Demo is true, adding two or three believable contract-example-based rows to every contract-backed domain table, while allowing duplicates on repeated runs and adding no demo rows when the setting is false or unset.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Configure Seed:Demo as false in the test factory unless demo seeding is explicitly requested.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Use 2,000 pounds per ton when normalizing inventory, ration, and feeding quantities and unit costs, while retaining entered units and quantities for display.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Deliver the feedlot functionality through HTTP API operations without separate product screens in this repository, leaving browser-visible pages for API documentation or health information only.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-7 has an anchor that doesn't match the code\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}